# Project Refactoring & Upgrade Rules

## Review & Audit Phase
- Always analyze code dependencies and usages before suggesting removals.
- Highlight unused exports, dead code, and redundant packages.

## Trimming Rules
- Do not remove code without explicit approval in Plan Mode first.
- Keep structural commits atomic: separate code trimming/deletion from upgrading/refactoring.

## Upgrade Standards
- Verify breaking changes for dependency upgrades before editing package configs.
- Run type checks or linter checks (`npm run check` or `tsc --noEmit`) after every major file change.